 lists DH 499; the reader found it not in the text.","where":"Cerritos College''s program record in the state''s curriculum inventory"},{"kind":"Catalog and state file differ","owner":"college","text":"The catalog prints COMM C1004, COMM 125 for this program; the state''s Program Course File does not list them.","where":"Cerritos College''s program record in the state''s curriculum inventory"},{"kind":"Check not met","owner":"procedure","text":"The blocks add to 114-116.5 units; the catalog prints 120-122 units.","where":"Cerritos College''s CourseLeaf reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"The catalog text begins mid-way through an outcomes/goals list; the first visible line (''s and professional associations.'') is a truncated fragment and was not recorded. The heading of that list is not in the text, so a reviewer should confirm whether these lines are program learning outcomes, program goals or competencies. The lines beginning ''To encourage...'' and ''To defend...'' read like program goals rather than outcomes.","where":"Cerritos College''s CourseLeaf reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"Lower division also requires ''*Biochemistry or Organic Chemistry with Biochemistry'' (4.0-5.0 units). It has no course code because Cerritos does not offer it and it must be taken at another institution, so it is not recorded as a course.","where":"Cerritos College''s CourseLeaf reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"The lower division block prints ''Total Units for Lower Division Coursework 26-27'' under the table, but the summary at the end prints 26.0-27.5. The block''s stated value uses the table figure.","where":"Cerritos College''s CourseLeaf reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"The 4.0-4.5 range is printed on the PSYC 210 row and covers the statistics choice as a whole (PSYC 210, STAT C1000, STAT C1000E or ECON 210). Units are not printed beside the alternatives.","where":"Cerritos College''s CourseLeaf reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"The catalog prints SOCI C1000; the closed list stores it as ''SOCIC1000'' with no units. This is treated as the same course.","where":"Cerritos College''s CourseLeaf reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"DH 315C and DH 432L appear in the closed list as ''DH 315c'' and ''DH 432l''. These are treated as the same courses.","where":"Cerritos College''s CourseLeaf reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"COMM C1004 and COMM 125 appear as alternatives to COMM 100 but are not on the closed list. COMM C1000 is titled ''Introduction to Public Speaking'' in the catalog.","where":"Cerritos College''s CourseLeaf reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"The upper division courses are printed by term (Semester One, Semester Two, Summer Semester, Semester Three, Semester Four). They are recorded as one required block totaling the stated 66 units.","where":"Cerritos College''s CourseLeaf reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"The total of 120-122 units includes 15 elective units ''to meet the minimum of 120 units''. General education is completed before applying and is not counted in the listed coursework totals.","where":"Cerritos College''s CourseLeaf reading procedure"},{"kind":"Reader''s note","owner":"procedure","text":"The lower division science prerequisites carry recency, GPA and wet-lab requirements; see the catalog text.","where":"Cerritos College''s CourseLeaf reading procedure"}],"map":{"checked_run":"census-20261004T152831Z-s3of4","host":null,"status":"none","text":"The weekly census found no published term-by-term program map on Cerritos College''s site (census run census-20261004T152831Z-s3of4).","url":null},"v":1}'::jsonb from public.program_requirement_records r where r.college = 'Cerritos 